<title>HONG KONG: HK-Melbourne air cargo down 17pct in yr to end-Oct.</title>
<headline>HK-Melbourne air cargo down 17pct in yr to end-Oct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Hong Kong/Melbourne air route fell 17.1 per cent in the amount of freight in the year to end-October 1996, latest statistics issued by Australia's Department of Transport and Regional Development show.</p>
<p>Auckland/Sydney remained Australia's busiest city to city air freight route for the same period despite showing a 0.2 per cent decrease to 41,631 tonnes for the year up to October 1996.</p>
<p>Hong Kong/Sydney was the second busiest city pair reporting a 9.6 per cent rise in the amount of freight carried to 36,605 tonnes for the same period.</p>
<p>The Department said the top ten city pairs listed below represented 49 per cent of total freight tonnes traffic for the year to October compared with 49.9 per cent for the year to October 1995 and 50.4 per cent for the year to October 1994.  City Pair	    Year ended				  PctChange</p>
<p>				Oct 96   Oct 95   Oct 94	   96 over 95</p>
<p> Auckland/Sydney	  41,631   41,712   42,646	  -0.2</p>
<p> Hong Kong/Sydney	 36,605   33,393   25,741	   9.6</p>
<p> Singapore/Sydney	 35,792   33,187   31,044	   7.9</p>
<p> Auckland/Melbourne     32,218   23,497   21,902	  37.1</p>
<p> Singapore/Melbourne    29,155   29,428   25,158	  -0.9</p>
<p> Los Angeles/Sydney     29,102   32,586   31,367	 -10.7</p>
<p> Hong Kong/Melbourne    23,471   28,298   21,903	 -17.1</p>
<p> Tokyo/Sydney	     21,671   21,787   24,957	  -0.5</p>
<p> Singapore/ Perth	 20,367   18,790   18,706	   8.4</p>
<p> Auckland/ Brisbane     12,651   11,469   11,368	  10.3</p>
<p> Other city pairs	294,583  275,399  251,032	   7.0</p>
<p> All City Pairs	  577,248  549,547  505,825	   5.0</p>
